    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d507">

                <pb facs="0694" n="595" xml:id="pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.1431/164: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Chargé in Guatemala</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">O’Donoghue</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-21T14:00:00-05:00">March 21, 1936—2 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>16. Referring to the Legation’s telegram No. 23, March 18, noon.</p>
                <list>
                    <label>1.</label>
                    <item>If Guatemala insists on insertion the Department prefers that “by
                        exporter” be replaced by “made in the country of export.”</item>
                    <label>2.</label>
                    <item>Language quoted appears acceptable except that use of word “special” has
                        restrictive connotation hence the Department would like to have it omitted
                        or replaced by “other”.</item>
                    <label>3.</label>
                    <item>The Department hopes to have texts ready for submission to you by airmail
                        next week.</item>
                </list>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
